      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I chose an Aussie system because it is more robust and designed for our climate and harsh weather. I like that each panel has it own mini invertor making each independent from others and unlike an inline one invertor system still produces electricity and delivers it to the home even if panels are down. Production can be monitored via my internet and will immediately indicate if panels are down.This activity is also accessed by the installer who can correct or address any failings immediately. I've had no issues with the system unlike imports where after receiving quarterly accounts, found no production during that time. With no Govt. buy back and only low offerings from power suppliers, Power generated through the day powers the house and I only sell the excess to the retailer.This way we use all heavy users of power, like dishwasher, washing machine during that time. Aussie Solar a local company, was very helpful and completed the installation in a timely, professional manner.",
